<title>USA: US, Japan insurance differences &quot;significant&quot;.</title>
<headline>US, Japan insurance differences &quot;significant&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States and Japan remain far apart in negotiations to resolve a dispute over deregulation of insurance in Japan, a U.S. trade official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The distance between our positions is still significant,&quot; a trade official told reporters.  He said he would not characterize himself as either optimistic or pessimistic about talks this week in Tokyo aimed at resolving the trade dispute.</p>
<p>The United States has accused Japan of reneging on a 1994 agreement that calls for opening primary life and casualty markets dominated by big Japanese insurance firms before deregulating the smaller specialty market in which foreign firms enjoy a big share.</p>
</text>
